{
  "title": "79: al-Naazea'at النازعات",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنّٰزِعٰتِ غَرْقًا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy those [angels] who wrest [the soul] violently,\nوَّالنّٰشِطٰتِ نَشْطًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nby those who draw [it] out gently,\nوَّالسّٰبِحٰتِ سَبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nby those who swim smoothly,\nفَالسّٰبِقٰتِ سَبْقًا ۙ‏(4)\n\nby those who, racing, take the lead,\nفَالْمُدَبِّرٰتِ اَمْرًا‌ ۘ‏(5)\n\nby those who direct the affairs [of creatures]:\nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الرَّاجِفَةُ ۙ‏(6)\n\nthe day when the Quaker quakes\nتَتْبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُ ؕ‏(7)\n\nand is followed by the Successor,\nقُلُوْبٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّاجِفَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\n\nhearts will be trembling on that day,\nاَبْصَارُهَا خَاشِعَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(9)\n\nbearing a humbled look.\nيَقُوْلُوْنَ ءَاِنَّا لَمَرْدُوْدُوْنَ فِى الْحَافِرَةِ ؕ‏(10)\n\nThey will say, ‘Are we being returned to our earlier state?\nءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا نَّخِرَةً ؕ‏(11)\n\nWhat, even after we have been decayed bones?!’\nقَالُوْا تِلْكَ اِذًا كَرَّةٌ خَاسِرَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\n\nThey will say, ‘This is, then, a ruinous return!’\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\n\nYet it will be only a single shout,\nفَاِذَا هُمْ بِالسَّاهِرَةِ ؕ‏(14)\n\nand behold, they will be awake.\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(15)\n\nDid you receive the story of Moses,\nاِذْ نَادٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى‌ۚ‏(16)\n\nwhen his Lord called out to him in the holy valley of Tuwa?\nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى ۖ‏(17)\n\n[And said,] ‘Go to Pharaoh, for indeed he has rebelled,\nفَقُلْ هَلْ لَّكَ اِلٰٓى اَنْ تَزَكّٰى ۙ‏(18)\n\nand say, ‘‘Would you purify yourself?\nوَاَهْدِيَكَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَتَخْشٰى‌ۚ‏(19)\n\nI will guide you to your Lord, that you may fear [Him]?’’ ’\nفَاَرٰٮهُ الْاٰيَةَ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(20)\n\nThen he showed him the greatest sign.\nفَكَذَّبَ وَعَصٰى ۖ‏(21)\n\nBut he denied, and disobeyed.\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ يَسْعٰىۖ‏(22)\n\nThen he turned back, walking swiftly,\nفَحَشَرَ فَنَادٰىۖ‏(23)\n\nand gathered [the people] and proclaimed,\nفَقَالَ اَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْاَعْلٰى ۖ‏(24)\n\nsaying, ‘I am your exalted lord!’\nفَاَخَذَهُ اللّٰهُ نَكَالَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَالْاُوْلٰى ؕ‏(25)\n\nSo Allah seized him with the punishment of this life and the Hereafter.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰىؕ‏(26)\n\nThere is indeed a moral in that for someone who fears!\nءَاَنْتُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمِ السَّمَآءُ‌ ؕ بَنٰٮهَا‏(27)\n\nIs your creation more prodigious or that of the heaven He has built?\nرَفَعَ سَمْكَهَا فَسَوَّٮهَا ۙ‏(28)\n\nHe raised its vault and fashioned it,\nوَ اَغْطَشَ لَيْلَهَا وَاَخْرَجَ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(29)\n\nand darkened its night, and brought forth its forenoon.\nوَالْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ دَحٰٮهَا ؕ‏(30)\n\nThereafter He spread out the earth,\nاَخْرَجَ مِنْهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرْعٰٮهَا‏(31)\n\nbrought forth from it its water and pastures,\nوَالْجِبَالَ اَرْسٰٮهَا ۙ‏(32)\n\nsetting firm the mountains,\nمَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(33)\n\nas a [place of] sustenance for you and your livestock.\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الطَّآمَّةُ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(34)\n\nWhen the Greatest Catastrophe befalls\nيَوْمَ يَتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(35)\n\n—the day when man will remember his endeavours\nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِمَنْ يَّرٰى‏(36)\n\nand hell is brought into view for those who can see—\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ طَغٰىۙ‏(37)\n\nas for him who has been rebellious\nوَاٰثَرَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ۙ‏(38)\n\nand preferred the life of this world,\nفَاِنَّ الْجَحِيْمَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(39)\n\nhis refuge will indeed be hell.\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ وَ نَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوٰىۙ‏(40)\n\nBut as for him who is awed to stand before his Lord and restrains his soul from [following] desires,\nفَاِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(41)\n\nhis refuge will indeed be paradise.\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ‏(42)\n\nThey ask you concerning the Hour, “When will it set in,\nفِيْمَ اَنْتَ مِنْ ذِكْرٰٮهَاؕ‏(43)\n\nconsidering your frequent mention of it?”\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ مُنْتَهٰٮهَاؕ‏(44)\n\nIts outcome is with your Lord.\nاِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰٮهَاؕ‏(45)\n\nYou are only a warner for those who are afraid it.\nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(46)\n\nThe day they see it, it shall be as if they had not stayed [in the world] except for an evening or forenoon.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naazea’at (Those Who Pull Out)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 42 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of entities in the Heavens."
